{
  "version": 1,
  "for": "WO-031 extension field accuracy on the captured application forms (tests/fixtures/forms-ci)",
  "annotator": "the WO-031 builder, by reading each question's text and options as an applicant would, before the extension's fills were measured; the planner's own mapping was not consulted for any entry",
  "persona": "evals/apply/fill-coverage.ts PERSONA (the complete synthetic TEST persona), minus eeo (this persona gave no voluntary self-identification) and resume (the file the extension attaches)",
  "rules": [
    "Each bound field (scripts/career/form-bind.ts, by its name) names the persona fact it asks, or null when the persona has no answer for it and it must stay empty, or \"any\" when filling the persona's value and leaving it empty are both right.",
    "null covers: voluntary self-identification (EEO, demographics, surveys), essays and free comments, questions about another person, follow-ups to an answer the persona did not give (\"If yes...\", \"If other...\"), questions about this job no persona fact answers (a location choice, a pay rate, an exam), and a stated value that does not fit the field's format (\"2 weeks\" in a date field).",
    "A single checkbox whose right answer is no is null: unchecked is right whether or not the extension touched it.",
    "Expected value, computed by tests/career-extension-browser.test.cjs expectedValue(): a file field is the resume's file name; a field with options is the option whose text equals the persona's value, else for a yes/no fact the one option starting with that yes or no, else the entry's explicit expect; a single checkbox is 'Yes (checked)' for yes and 'No' for no; anything else is the persona's value as stated.",
    "An entry {fact, expect} gives the exact expected value where the rule above cannot (a graduation year from a graduation date, an option worded unlike the persona's value)."
  ],
  "split": {
    "rule": "per family, the two captured forms with the lowest sha256(id) are held out; the rest are dev. Reader changes are made only from dev results; the held-out forms are measured, never tuned on.",
